# Task 6 Linux control-plane failure-path evidence
# Captured: 2026-08-22

## Red test before implementation

Command: `cargo test -p wifimic_server control -- --nocapture`
Result: EXPECTED FAIL before the state machine existed. The compiler reported unresolved
`CaptureController`, `ControlPlane`, `ControlState`, and `CaptureError` imports in the focused
tests. This established the red test seam rather than a test typo or runtime failure.

## Rejection and timeout failure paths

Command: `cargo test -p wifimic_server control_rejects_stale_or_replayed_session_id -- --nocapture`
Result: PASS — 1 passed, 0 failed. A stale Start produced no Ack, did not change state, and
did not start capture; the Stop high-water mark remains available to reject delayed replay.

Command: `cargo test -p wifimic_server control_stops_capture_after_30s_without_heartbeat -- --nocapture`
Result: PASS — 1 passed, 0 failed. An injected time beyond the 30-second deadline transitioned
Streaming to Idle, stopped the fake capture exactly once, and emitted HeartbeatTimeout.

Adversarial checks in `cargo test -p wifimic_server control -- --nocapture` also passed for
mismatched Heartbeat/Stop IDs and old-session Heartbeat after Streaming supersession. Rejected
commands returned no Ack and emitted typed ControlMessageRejected diagnostics.

